  "$reasons": {
    "ignore.*.code": "Behaviour-only props (open state, dismissal, a11y role tweaks, layout stretch) with no visual counterpart in a Figma component.",
    "ignore.<split set>.code": "Figma splits one code component into several sets (Inline/Rich toast, Search/Search ghost, Combobox/Combobox multi, Sidebar selector icon/label, Date picker popover/inline). The discriminating code prop is the set itself.",
    "components.Scrollbar": "Native/OS scrollbar styling only — no React component.",
    "props.Badge.Label": "Badge renders a numeric `count`; Figma's Label text is that count.",
    "ignore.Button.code": "`type` is the native HTML button type (submit/reset), not a visual variant.",
    "components.<item sets>": "Breadcrumb item, Segment control selector, Navigation tab and Custom view tab are single items; in code they are entries of the parent's items/options/tabs array, whose item types are not extracted into ds-index.json. Check these by hand.",
    "values.Standard": "Badge: Figma \"Standard\" is the numeric badge, code size `sm` (the other size is `dot`).",
    "values.Empty / Partially filled": "OTPInput: Figma shows empty and partly-typed states; in code both are status `idle` (fill comes from `value`).",
    "values.Max value": "Slider: Figma \"Max value\" is the single-thumb slider, code mode `single`.",
    "values.<Field type labels>": "DataTableCell: Figma uses descriptive field-type labels (Phone number, Tags read-only…); code uses short kebab ids (phone, tags-readonly…).",
    "ignore.Data table / Cell / Header cell": "Figma sets sort direction by swapping the arrow icon instance (INSTANCE_SWAP); code has a `sortDirection` union that renders that icon. Same concept, different modelling.",
    "ignore.Choice list.code": "`enableMenuKeyboardNavigation` is keyboard behaviour only.",
    "ignore.Data table / Cell / Header cell.code (reorder, checkbox)": "`canMoveReorderLeft/Right` only enable column-menu items; `checkboxChecked/Indeterminate` set the nested Checkbox instance, which Figma configures on the instance itself.",
    "ignore.Data table / Cell / Table cell.code": "`revealActionsOnHover` is hover behaviour; Figma shows the revealed state via the cell variant.",
    "ignore.Toolbar.code": "`singleActionFullWidth` is a layout stretch, same as the global `fullWidth` ignore.",
    "ignore.Menu cell.code": "`switcherChecked` sets the nested Switcher instance, which Figma configures on the instance itself.",
    "ignore.*.figma (scroll bars)": "Figma draws scroll bars as toggleable layers to mock overflow; code uses native overflow scrolling (see components.Scrollbar).",
    "ignore.Button group.figma": "`Amount` previews 2/3/4+ buttons; in code the count is the number of children.",
    "ignore.Input / Horizontal input.figma": "`Change input type` swaps the nested input instance; in code the input is passed as a child.",
    "ignore.Data table / Cell / Table cell.figma": "TEXT properties are per-field-type content placeholders; code renders `value`/children.",
    "ignore.<inputs>.figma (Show actions / Show clear button)": "Design-time affordances on input sets: trailing actions and the clear button are composed by the consumer in code (e.g. passed as `trailingIcon`), not toggled by a boolean prop. Decided 2026-10-15 in /ds-component-sync."
  }
